> x mud
Grey, glutinous and ankle-deep in the hollows, worked to a slick paste by the
water running through it. Your boots have no purchase in it whatsoever.

> n
You attempt to march past the sentinels, but as you step between them, an
invisible force like compressed air slams against your chest, throwing you back
into the tunnel. The statues remain motionless, watching.

> cast animate on warrior
The spellbook opens itself to the right page, and you read aloud the complicated
words of the animation spell.

The statue comes to life!

The warrior attacks you and aims at your chest. You manage to squirm past him.

> cast animate on barbarian
The spellbook opens itself to the right page, and you read aloud the complicated
words of the animation spell.

The statue comes to life!

The warrior and the barbarian fight each other. The swords clash, but both are
still unharmed.

> cast freeze on mud
The spellbook opens itself to the right page, and you read aloud the complicated
words of the freeze spell.

The temperature drops at once. The water and the mud freeze hard, your boots go
out from under you, and you slither a couple of metres down the tunnel before
you can stop yourself.

The warrior and the barbarian trade blows across the frozen floor, and neither
of them has landed one yet.

The warrior and the barbarian slip on the ice at the same moment and go down the
slope together. The barbarian grabs at your leg on the way past, and takes you
with him.

The Dragon Hall
You slide to a stop in a vast hall cut straight out of the heart of the
mountain. The stench of sulfur is oppressive, and the floor lies under a layer
of ash deep enough to say that no mortal has set foot here for centuries. The
only way out is the treacherous, muddy incline behind you.

Sprawled across a staggering hoard of gold and priceless relics is a colossal
dragon.

The dragon tilts her massive head, watching your sudden and undignified entrance
with frank curiosity.

You can also see a barbarian and a warrior here.

> x dragon
Whole again, she is magnificent and frankly terrifying: a long, deep-chested
body of overlapping bronze scales, and a pair of eyes that consider you with
perfect, unhurried intelligence.

The warrior and the barbarian see the dragon and rush forward with weapons
drawn. She takes the warrior first and he goes up like dry kindling, but the
barbarian is inside her guard before she can turn, and drives his sword deep
into her throat. Beside herself with rage and pain, she burns what is left of
the pair of them to ash.

> x it
The spell reads "freeze spell: freeze something."

The dragon is almost dead.

> cast healing on dragon
The spellbook opens itself to the right page, and you read aloud the complicated
words of the healing spell.

The blood stops flowing and the wound in her throat closes. The dragon is still
in shock, but you have saved her life.

The dragon lies where she fell, flanks heaving, and does not seem to have
noticed you at all yet.

