A yellow cloud surrounds you, and as it clears you find yourself in the...

Meadow
You stand in a small, overgrown clearing dominated by a dilapidated hut hunched
immediately to the south. Looming on all other sides is a dense, ancient forest
whose twisted boughs form an impenetrable wall of shadow. A faint dirt path cuts
through the weeds, winding away north into the dark tree line.

> s
As you enter the hut your old mentor says, "I see you have found more stones.
Very good. If you keep up this pace we shall soon be done. Put the stones in the
gilded box."

Hut
The interior of the hut is cramped and gloomy. Thick soot cakes the solitary
window, leaving the flickering flames of a stone hearth as the room's sole
source of light. Atop the fire, rusted iron vessels bubble quietly, venting
strange, multi-coloured vapours. A massive, cluttered workbench is buried under
a chaotic heap of heavy grimoires, brittle sheets of paper, and exotic
alchemical ingredients. A heavy wooden door leads north, back out to the forest
path.

Resting within a small alcove in the stone wall is a beautifully carved, gilded
wooden box. It contains a black stone.

Your mentor reads a parchment.

> x parchment
It reads: "The resurrection spell -- raise the dead." The spell itself runs on
for a great many lines, and every one of them is more complicated than the last.

> put stones in box
blue stone: You put the blue stone into the gilded box.
green stone: You put the green stone into the gilded box.
red stone: Your mentor sees you place the last stone in the box and cries, "The
last stone! Now I can open the gate!"

He takes the stones out of the box and says, "Come with me. Great tasks await."
Everything turns yellow as he reads a teleportation spell, and you are carried
away to another place.

The Crypt
The chamber has the look of a heathen temple. Obsidian pillars rise into the
darkness, carved with blasphemous runes that seem to shift whenever you are not
looking straight at them. A great stone altar stands at the centre, stained dark
by old rituals, and four glowing pedestals surround it. There are no exits.

Your mentor stands before you.

Istar's familiar, kindly features suddenly warp and contort. His skin blackens
and splits, his eyes igniting with a hellish, crimson fire as his bones snap out
of place. Before you stands a towering, grotesque demon, its voice echoing like
grinding stones:

"At last, I have you right where I want you! Your precious mentor was a fool...
far too curious for his own good. The moment he began dabbling in the dark arts,
he practically invited me in. Snaring his soul was trivial. His snobbish
colleagues at the Academy were sharper than you; they sensed my presence,
forcing me to flee to this wretched wilderness. Because their inquisitors hunted
me, I could not gather the stones myself. I needed a naive pawn to fetch the
keys to open the gateway... not to white magic, you poor blind thing, but to
unleash the Old Gods whom I serve!

I searched your mentor's memories and found you. I knew you would come when he
called, and now you have carried me the key to your own doom. Was it not a fine
plan?"

"Now to work. First a small precaution," says the demon, and you are trapped in
a red force field.

> x field
A shimmering sphere of translucent red energy surrounds you completely,
crackling with raw, dark magic. Touching it causes a sharp, burning shock.

The demon reads a spell aloud.

The amulet begins to vibrate.

> x amulet
The beggar's little amulet is shaking against your breastbone hard enough to
hurt, and it has gone hot. It is straining away from you on its cord, towards
the red light, the way a compass needle strains towards north.

Part of the floor falls away, and a dark opening like a well appears. There is a
slimy liquid standing in it. Still reading, the demon begins to pace anti-
clockwise around the well.

The amulet vibrates violently.

> touch field with amulet
The amulet meets the red field, and the field goes out like a snuffed candle!

The Crypt
The chamber has the look of a heathen temple. Obsidian pillars rise into the
darkness, carved with blasphemous runes that seem to shift whenever you are not
looking straight at them. A great stone altar stands at the centre, stained dark
by old rituals, and four glowing pedestals surround it. There are no exits.


The demon drops the stones one by one into the well, and the liquid sinks away.

